WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.259
The machine keeping a patient breathing can also expose

00:00:04.259 --> 00:00:07.025
delicate airway cells to damaging forces.

00:00:10.925 --> 00:00:15.037
We modelled one mechanical event in cultured rat alveolar

00:00:15.037 --> 00:00:18.789
epithelial cells: a single air bubble passing over a

00:00:18.789 --> 00:00:19.510
monolayer.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.906
We used a parallel-plate chamber, fluorescence live-dead

00:00:27.906 --> 00:00:31.448
staining, and microscopy to examine what happened after

00:00:31.448 --> 00:00:32.672
bubble propagation.

00:00:37.383 --> 00:00:40.613
Our experiment tested whether pretreatment with

00:00:40.613 --> 00:00:44.393
dexamethasone or trans-dehydroandrosterone could change

00:00:44.393 --> 00:00:47.280
the cells' susceptibility before exposure.

00:00:52.675 --> 00:00:56.217
Under these in-vitro conditions, bubble flow injured

00:00:56.217 --> 00:00:59.895
cells. Pretreatment significantly reduced the measured

00:00:59.895 --> 00:01:03.436
cell death, alongside changes in cellular mechanics.

00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:13.027
A culture chamber is not a ventilated patient. The result

00:01:13.027 --> 00:01:16.436
is a mechanistic finding and a question for further

00:01:16.436 --> 00:01:19.177
translation, not a clinical prescription.
